{"pageId":"e13272c803cad5da","url":"https://cms.gov/newsroom/fact-sheets/open-enrollment-trends-selected-healthcaregov-statistics-prior-january-1-2016-coverage-deadline","week":"2026-W35","runId":"2026-08-28T16-47-00-206Z-3b5fd8","scannedAt":"2026-08-28T16:59:59.811Z","status":200,"depth":9,"axe":{"engine":"axe-core","version":"4.12.1","violationCount":0,"violations":{},"incompleteCount":19},"plainLanguage":{"engine":"plain-language","scored":true,"scoreSkipReason":null,"wordCount":661,"misspelledCount":1,"misspelled":["Howden"],"sentenceCount":21,"fleschReadingEase":51.5,"fleschKincaidGrade":13.9,"avgSentenceLength":31.5,"longSentences":13,"passiveVoiceRatio":0,"unexplainedAcronyms":["OE","CMS"],"unexplainedAcronymCount":2},"resources":{"engine":"resources","count":0,"byType":{},"resources":[]},"images":{"engine":"images","count":6,"images":[{"src":"https://www.cms.gov/themes/custom/cms_evo/logo.svg","alt":"CMS.gov","hasAlt":true,"isDecorative":false,"isMissingAlt":false,"ariaHidden":false,"rolePresentation":false,"renderedWidth":170,"renderedHeight":41,"naturalWidth":300,"naturalHeight":72,"loading":null,"decoding":null,"altVerdict":"GOOD","altReason":"present, no red flags","bytes":2086},{"src":"https://www.cms.gov/sites/default/files/styles/desktop_width/public/fact-sheets/2015-12-22.png?itok=zqASTivz","alt":"Nearly 6 Million Plan Selections Nov 1 – Dec 17. Through the deadline for January 1, 2016 coverage, almost 6 million people signed up for health coverage through HealthCare.gov, compared to last year when about 3.4 million had signed up by the first enrollment deadline. Of the nearly 6 million total consumers already enrolled for 2016 coverage, 2.4 million are new consumers, compared to 1.8 million new consumers in the same period for OE2.  Note: The OE2 and OE3 figures do not include anyone auto-enrolled for January 1 coverage.","hasAlt":true,"isDecorative":false,"isMissingAlt":false,"ariaHidden":false,"rolePresentation":false,"renderedWidth":715,"renderedHeight":444,"naturalWidth":715,"naturalHeight":444,"loading":"lazy","decoding":null,"altVerdict":"TOO_LONG","altReason":"alt text is 534 characters — consider a caption or description","bytes":67353},{"src":"https://www.cms.gov/sites/default/files/styles/desktop_width/public/fact-sheets/2015-12-22-2.png?itok=Mmv_nDJT","alt":"Consumers Are Younger: The average age of a consumer in OE3 is lower through the deadline for January 1st coverage this year than through the deadline in OE2. In fact, there are nearly twice as many consumers under the age of 35 ahead of the deadline for January 1 coverage this year compared to last. By the end of the first deadline this year (Dec 17), there were about 2.1 million HealthCare.gov consumers under 35 years old, compared to about 1.1 million before the first deadline last year. Those under 35 comprised 35% of Healthcare.gov consumers by the end of the first deadline this year, compared to 33% before the deadline last year for January 1 coverage.","hasAlt":true,"isDecorative":false,"isMissingAlt":false,"ariaHidden":false,"rolePresentation":false,"renderedWidth":624,"renderedHeight":358,"naturalWidth":624,"naturalHeight":358,"loading":"lazy","decoding":null,"altVerdict":"TOO_LONG","altReason":"alt text is 666 characters — consider a caption or description","bytes":40763},{"src":"https://www.cms.gov/sites/default/files/styles/desktop_width/public/fact-sheets/2015-12-22-3.png?itok=gQD4CQ_4","alt":"There are more new young consumers this year than last year: at the end of the first deadline (Dec 17), there were about 980 thousand new Healthcare.gov consumers under 35 years. That compares to about 670 thousand before the first deadline last year. Put another way: those under 35 comprised 41% of new Healthcare.gov consumers by the end of the first deadline this year (Dec 17), compared to 38% before the deadline last year.","hasAlt":true,"isDecorative":false,"isMissingAlt":false,"ariaHidden":false,"rolePresentation":false,"renderedWidth":60